Third-party material
--------------------

Part of the German vocabulary in this dictionary was gathered from the German
quest text in the quest database of Questie
(https://github.com/Questie/Questie), which is distributed under the GNU
General Public License version 3.

Modifications made by Ironship, 30 August 2026:

  * German quest titles and objective lines for Classic Era were read for the
    words they contain. Roughly 3,900 words that the dictionary did not
    already cover were taken from them.
  * What this addon ships is not that text. It is a list of individual German
    words, each with an English translation and an explanatory note written
    for this project. No quest sentence is reproduced.
  * The remaining ~74,000 entries were built from Blizzard's own Game Data API
    and are unaffected.

The extraction is performed by Tools/extract_classic_words.py, which is part of
the corresponding source of this work.

A further part of the vocabulary was gathered from the German quest text in the
MultiLanguage addon by Ruben Zantingh
(https://github.com/rubenzantingh/MultiLanguage), used with his permission
given on 2 September 2026.

Blizzard's Game Data API publishes a quest's title and description and nothing
else, so until now this dictionary held 52 objective lines and 13 progress
lines against 28,888 descriptions. MultiLanguage carries the objective line,
the text an NPC speaks while a quest is in progress, and the text spoken when
it is handed in, for more quests than the API returns.

Modifications made by Ironship, 2 September 2026:

  * That text was read for the words it contains: 36,405 objective lines,
    11,094 progress lines and 26,246 hand-in lines, covering 16,888 quests the
    API does not return at all.
  * As above, what this addon ships is not that text. Quest text stays in
    Data/cache, which is outside the repository and is never packaged. What
    ships is a list of single words, each with an English translation and an
    explanatory note written for this project. No quest sentence is reproduced.
  * Where Blizzard's API had already supplied a field, its wording was kept.

The import is performed by Tools/import_multilanguage.py, which is part of the
corresponding source of this work.

